messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/dbs/xtiff/xtiff.c
Line: 1268
Function: EventProc
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: In the Expose case, sx/sy are set to dx+xOffset/dy+yOffset, while w/h are set to MIN(event->xexpose.width, iw) and MIN(event->xexpose.height, ih). When a fake Expose event is posted with width/height equal to the full image size (e.g., in ResizeProc at lines 1304-1309) and xOffset/yOffset > 0, this results in sx + w > image width (or sy + h > image height). The subsequent XPutImage call at line 1268 reads past the bounds of xImage->data, causing an out-of-bounds read and potential crash. This occurs when appData.usePixmap == False.

Source context:
```c
     1228:                     if (next_event.type == MotionNotify)
     1229:                         return;
     1230:             if ((grabX < 0) || (grabY < 0))
     1231:                 return;
     1232:             sx = xOffset + grabX - (int)event->xmotion.x;
     1233:             if (sx >= (iw - ww)) /* clamp x motion but allow y motion */
     1234:                 sx = iw - ww;
     1235:             sx = MAX(sx, 0);
     1236:             sy = yOffset + grabY - (int)event->xmotion.y;
     1237:             if (sy >= (ih - wh)) /* clamp y motion but allow x motion */
     1238:                 sy = ih - wh;
     1239:             sy = MAX(sy, 0);
     1240:             if ((sx == xOffset) && (sy == yOffset))
     1241:                 return;
     1242:             dx = dy = 0;
     1243:             w = ww;
     1244:             h = wh;
     1245:             break;
     1246:         case ButtonRelease:
     1247:             xOffset = xOffset + grabX - (int)event->xbutton.x;
     1248:             xOffset = MIN(iw - ww, xOffset);
     1249:             xOffset = MAX(xOffset, 0);
     1250:             yOffset = yOffset + grabY - (int)event->xbutton.y;
     1251:             yOffset = MIN(ih - wh, yOffset);
     1252:             yOffset = MAX(yOffset, 0);
     1253:             grabX = grabY = -1;
     1254:         default:
     1255:             return;
